{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-177757",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the phrase \"it is a multiple of $2$ and $5$\" as the equivalent phrase \"it is a multiple of $2$ and it is a multiple of $5.$\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$n$ is a multiple of $2,$ and it is a multiple of $2$ and  it is a multiple of $5.$\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$n$ is a multiple of $2$ and it is a multiple of $2,$ and  it is a multiple of $5.$\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$n$ is a multiple of $2$ and it is a multiple of $2$\" to just \"$n$ is a multiple of $2.$\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$n$ is a multiple of $2,$ and it is multiple of $5.$\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely as\n\n\"$n$ is a multiple of $2$ and $5.$\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
